BEGIN_TEXT
Training is a practice copy of the box. It has its own store, filled with
sample traffic: real-shaped MARS messages with made-up calls and routing
indicators, addressed to your call. You can read them, compose, reply and
send, and watch it all work.

While training is on:
 - TRAINING shows on line 2 of every screen.
 - Nothing goes on the air. What you send goes to a practice station
   inside the box, TRAIN-NCS, which acknowledges like a real one.
 - Your real traffic is kept apart: nothing you do here touches it, and
   your real station keeps receiving underneath.
 - Keys are practice keys, made for training. Your real tapes and cards
   are never used.
 - Resending stays in training too: a resend reaches the practice
   station only, never the radio, and your real store doesn't change.
 - If another screen on this box turns training on or off while you
   work, your next action is not done. The screen tells you which store
   is in force now; look, then do it again.

Turn training off to go back. The practice store stays until you reload
it, so you can pick up where you left off.
END
BEGIN_EXAMPLE
Turn training on. The In Box fills with about eighty sample messages, a
few overheard or garbled as on a real net, and three from TRAIN-NCS: a
welcome, a check-in request, and one sent enciphered in a practice key
that the box already holds. Answer the check-in: compose to TRAIN-NCS
and send. It is acknowledged and shows in the Out Box as acknowledged.
No radio was keyed.
END
